SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(b LIKE 'wb%') FROM wt2.z1 FORCE INDEX (kb);
COUNT(*)	SUM(b LIKE 'wb%')
23000	20000
# The worktree written and cloned again, three times: in overlay mode
# each clone freezes it again, and its overflow map pages stay in older
# layers (read through the stub's link, never from a layer's own holes).
UPDATE wt.z1 SET b = 'round1' WHERE id = 7;
CREATE WORKTREE wr1 FROM wt;
UPDATE wt.z1 SET b = 'round2' WHERE id = 7;
CREATE WORKTREE wr2 FROM wt;
UPDATE wt.z1 SET b = 'round3' WHERE id = 7;
CREATE WORKTREE wr3 FROM wt;
# restart
SELECT b FROM wr1.z1 WHERE id = 7;
b
round1
SELECT b FROM wr3.z1 WHERE id = 7;
b
round3
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM wr3.z1 FORCE INDEX (kb) WHERE b LIKE 'b1%';
COUNT(*)
1111
